    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section discusses the impact of aging on body image and sexual health, reviewing four previous studies. Augustus-Horvath and Tylka (2011) found midlife women had less body appreciation than emerging adults. Swami, Hadji-Michael, and Furnham (2008a) reported a small negative correlation between age and body appreciation in young British women. In contrast, Tiggemann and McCourt (2013) and Swami, Tran, Stieger, and Voracek (2014) found positive correlations between age and body appreciation, with the latter involving 9667 Western women. The section concludes by outlining the current paper's aim to investigate body appreciation as a buffer against age effects on sexual distress and satisfaction.",
